# Settings for watching Pakske on the Pi. Copy to ~/.config/pakske-watch.env and fill in.
# Keep it readable by you only: chmod 600. deploy/watch.sh, backup.sh and deploy.sh read it.
# What each setting means: docs/deploying.md, "Knowing when something is down".

# From healthchecks.io, under the project's Settings: the ping key, which lets the Pi report,
# and a read-write API key, which `deploy/watch.sh setup` uses to make the checks.
HC_PING_KEY=
HC_API_KEY=

# What to fetch every minute, as name=address pairs with a space between them. The name becomes
# the check's name: a-z, 0-9 and -. /api/health also asks the database a question.
WATCH_SITES=pakske=https://pakske.example.com/api/health
